  "chart choice line chart bar chart scatter plot histogram pie chart stacked bar visualisation best practices axis colour",
  "The right chart depends on the question: change over time, comparing categories, showing a distribution, or showing a relationship.",
  "Use a line chart for trends over time, a bar chart to compare categories (sorted, horizontal when labels are long), a histogram or box plot for distributions, and a scatter plot for the relationship between two numeric variables. Pie charts only work for a few parts of one whole; bars are usually clearer. Stacked bars make only the bottom segment easy to compare. Start bar axes at zero, label directly instead of relying on legends, use colour to highlight the point rather than decorate, and put the main message in the title.",
