  "pandas dataframe series read_csv loc iloc groupby agg merge join filter boolean indexing sort_values pivot_table python",
  "pandas is Python's main library for tabular data. A DataFrame is a table of named columns, and most analysis is filtering, grouping, joining and reshaping it.",
  "Read data with read_csv or read_parquet. Select columns by name, filter rows with boolean conditions, and use loc for label-based selection and iloc for position-based selection. groupby with agg is SQL's GROUP BY, merge is a join (with how='left' and friends), sort_values orders rows, and pivot_table reshapes long data into a wide table. Vectorised operations on whole columns are much faster than looping over rows with iterrows or apply. Watch for chained assignment warnings, and use .copy() when you mean to modify a slice.",
